{"nodes": [{"id": "vault_research_engine_dj_write_back_research", "label": "Engine DJ: what writing back to it involves (research)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "vault/research/engine-dj-write-back.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "vault_research_engine_dj_write_back_playlist_tree", "label": "The playlist tree is the same in every Engine DJ database", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "vault/research/engine-dj-write-back.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "763 playlists and 24,872 entries in each of the three copies read (C:, F:, G:), entries naming their song's database. How Engine DJ reconciles them, and what a drive not plugged in gets later, is [UNVERIFIED]; inferred from the counts that it reconciles each list to its latest edit."}, {"id": "vault_research_engine_dj_write_back_aggregating_drives", "label": "Engine DJ 5.3 Aggregating drives", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "vault/research/engine-dj-write-back.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "On every start 5.3 merges each connected drive's library into the Collection in one long write transaction, renumbers a drive's entries, and copies new Collection playlists with the Collection's parent ids. A loop of parent ids grew the merge to 13 GB; with three near-identical libraries the merge grew without end. Found in Engine DJ's logs and the databases."}, {"id": "vault_research_engine_dj_write_back_id_clash", "label": "Playlist id clash and drifted drive copies", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "vault/research/engine-dj-write-back.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Playlist 9047 is the user's list in C: and GLUE's Auto WONDA list in F:. 114 playlists' songs differed between C: and F:. Hypothesis [UNVERIFIED]: a new list that Engine DJ cannot make in a drive's copy stays locked."}, {"id": "vault_research_engine_dj_write_back_performance_data", "label": "Cues, loops and beat grid blobs (PerformanceData)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "vault/research/engine-dj-write-back.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Encoded to match libdjinterop: quickCues and beatData compressed (4-byte big-endian length then zlib), loops uncompressed and little-endian, positions in samples. The trackData layout beyond its sample rate is [UNVERIFIED]."}, {"id": "vault_research_engine_dj_write_back_subst_test", "label": "Library of GLUE's own shown as drive Z: (test of 2026-11-26)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "vault/research/engine-dj-write-back.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Seen at start with its songs playable by path and whole path; changes while closed reached the Collection at the next start; deleted, renamed and nested lists behaved as Engine DJ's own. A song whose file is gone is listed and will not play."}, {"id": "vault_research_engine_dj_write_back_engine_kb", "label": "Engine DJ Knowledge Base: third-party rules", "file_type": "paper", "source_file": "vault/research/engine-dj-write-back.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": "https://support.enginedj.com/support/solutions/articles/69000834165", "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Engine DJ's rules for third-party tools: do not open the database while Engine DJ runs, never change the schema, identify songs by (originDatabaseUuid, originTrackId)."}, {"id": "vault_research_engine_dj_write_back_libdjinterop", "label": "libdjinterop (blob encoders)", "file_type": "paper", "source_file": "vault/research/engine-dj-write-back.md", "source_location": 